For at least the next twelve months, there will be exactly one frontier AI asset that money can actually buy.

@AnthropicAI filed confidentially with the SEC in June. Goldman, Morgan Stanley, and JPMorgan are running it, investor meetings are being scheduled, and the window points to October. Shareholders are modeling a price above $2 trillion — which would make it the largest IPO in human history, past @SpaceX, past everything.

@OpenAI filed its S-1 too, then signaled 2027, with @sama reportedly treating anything under $1T as unacceptable.

So here's how I've been thinking about it: the bell doesn't just price one company. It reprices every link in the chain underneath — every wafer, every optical module, every megawatt, every model company, every SaaS seat. This thread walks the chain layer by layer. 🧵

